($q$University of Tasmania$q$, $q$Tasmanian Aurora Excellence Scholarship$q$, $q$Partial$q$, $q$Undergraduate$q$, $q$NOT YET CHECKED against the official page: this came from a web search and the figures may be wrong or out of date. Confirm on the official page before you rely on it. Requirements and Ghana eligibility: Highly competitive. Minimum ATAR 90 or equivalent. Requires eligibility for the International Merit Scholarship first, a 300 to 500-word personal statement and interview. The published WASSCE equivalency table does not provide an ATAR 90 equivalent, so a Ghanaian WASSCE applicant cannot confirm eligibility through that table alone. How to apply and deadline: Invitation after receiving an offer. Semester 1 2027 deadline 15 November 2026; Semester 2 deadline 30 April 2027. Direct entry with WASSCE: WASSCE accepted for undergraduate entry$q$, $q$50% tuition reduction for the course duration, up to five years.$q$, $q$https://www.utas.edu.au/study/scholarships-fees-and-costs/international-scholarships/tasmanian-international-merit-scholarship$q$),
