($q$University of Tasmania$q$, $q$Global Scholarships for International Students$q$, $q$Partial$q$, $q$Undergraduate and postgraduate$q$, $q$NOT YET CHECKED against the official page: this came from a web search and the figures may be wrong or out of date. Confirm on the official page before you rely on it. Requirements and Ghana eligibility: UTAS lists this external opportunity as open to international students across diploma, associate, bachelor’s, master’s, PhD and professional degrees. Exact nationality, academic and other eligibility conditions are set by the external provider, not stated in UTAS's summary. How to apply and deadline: Apply directly to Global Scholarships. Deadline not stated by UTAS. Direct entry with WASSCE: WASSCE accepted for undergraduate entry$q$, $q$AUD 3,000, one-off external award.$q$, $q$https://www.utas.edu.au/study/scholarships-fees-and-costs/international-scholarships$q$),
($q$University of Canberra$q$, $q$UC High Achievers Scholarship$q$, $q$Partial$q$, $q$Undergraduate$q$, $q$NOT YET CHECKED against the official page: this came from a web search and the figures may be wrong or out of date. Confirm on the official page before you rely on it. Requirements and Ghana eligibility: New international student entering an eligible undergraduate course at an Australian UC campus. Bachelor’s applicants need at least 80% or equivalent, or GPA 5.5/7. Ghana is explicitly included through the all-country eligibility. Excludes Nursing, Medical Imaging and specified other courses. How to apply and deadline: Automatic assessment when applying for admission. First-come, first-served until allocated places are filled. Direct entry with WASSCE: Not specifically stated in the admission sources checked. Ghana is recognised by UC for certain English-language exemptions when the qualification and medium-of-instruction conditions are met. That is not the same as confirming WASSCE academic admission equivalence. University of Canberra +1$q$, $q$20% tuition reduction.$q$, $q$https://www.canberra.edu.au/scholarship/uc-high-achievers$q$),
($q$University of Canberra$q$, $q$UC Merit Scholarship$q$, $q$Partial$q$, $q$Undergraduate$q$, $q$NOT YET CHECKED against the official page: this came from a web search and the figures may be wrong or out of date. Confirm on the official page before you rely on it. Requirements and Ghana eligibility: New international student in an eligible undergraduate course. Bachelor’s applicants need at least 70% or equivalent, or GPA 5/7. Ghana is included under all-country eligibility. Excludes specified courses, including Medical Imaging. How to apply and deadline: Automatic assessment with admission application. First-come, first-served. Direct entry with WASSCE: Not specifically stated in the admission sources checked. Ghana is recognised by UC for certain English-language exemptions when the qualification and medium-of-instruction conditions are met. That is not the same as confirming WASSCE academic admission equivalence. University of Canberra +1$q$, $q$10% tuition reduction.$q$, $q$https://www.canberra.edu.au/scholarship/uc-merit$q$),
($q$University of Canberra$q$, $q$UC Alumni Scholarships$q$, $q$Partial$q$, $q$Undergraduate$q$, $q$NOT YET CHECKED against the official page: this came from a web search and the figures may be wrong or out of date. Confirm on the official page before you rely on it. Requirements and Ghana eligibility: For international UC alumni returning to study. All alumni may be considered for 10%; the 30% level requires GPA 5.5/7 or at least 75% or equivalent. Ghanaian applicants qualify only if they meet the UC alumni condition. How to apply and deadline: Automatic assessment during admission. Direct entry with WASSCE: Not specifically stated in the admission sources checked. Ghana is recognised by UC for certain English-language exemptions when the qualification and medium-of-instruction conditions are met. That is not the same as confirming WASSCE academic admission equivalence. University of Canberra +1$q$, $q$10% or 30% tuition reduction.$q$, $q$https://www.canberra.edu.au/future-students/study-at-uc/international$q$),
